    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Papillary thyroid carcinoma, subtype with desmoid-type fibromatosis",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Nests of papillary carcinoma, oncocytic type, are embedded in an abundant stromal component made by spindle cells dispersed in a collagenous stroma resembling desmoid-type fibromatosis. The carcinomatous papillary thyroid carcinoma component showed the classic <em>BRAF</em> mutations (p.V600E), and the desmoid-type fibromatosis showed the &beta;-catenin <em>CTNNB1</em> mutation (p.S45P).",
    "source": "Massimo Bongiovanni",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/53/44/25787.jpg",
