    "chapterId": 44,
    "fileId": 28145,
    "type": "WSI",
    "diagnosis": "Papillary thyroid carcinoma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Columnar subtype. This infiltrative tumour is composed of columnar cells with pale eosinophilic cytoplasm showing prominent nuclear pseudostratification. There are subnuclear vacuoles. Nuclear clearing and grooves are focally noted. The cells are crowded into elongated follicles admixed with thin papillae.",
    "source": "Lester D.R. Thompson",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/28145.dzi",
